    title: "Israeli forces detain recently released prisoners in West Bank raids",
    summary: "Israeli forces detain recently released prisoners in West Bank raids Israeli forces have raided homes and arrested several Palestinians, including recently released prisoners, across the occupied West Bank, according to the Palestinian news agency Wafa. At dawn, soldiers arrested Muadh Nader Sawafta, 23, in the village of Tubas, and Naji Ibrahim Bisharat, 50, in the nearby town of Tammun, south of Tubas. Kamal Bani Odeh, director of the Palestinian Prisoners Society in Tubas, said that Sawafta had been released from Israeli detention two months ago. Israeli forces had detained 20 young men from the two villages the previous night, most of them from Tubas, before releasing them, the report said. In a separate raid on Friday, Israeli forces arrested three Palestinians in Qarawa Bani Hassan, southwest of Nablus. One of them was a former prisoner who had been released just two days earlier after spending two years in Israeli prisons, according to Wafa. Earlier on Friday, soldiers raided homes in the Iktaba neighbourhood, east of Tulkarem, and arrested three Palestinians. Local sources identified one of them as Jihad al-Qazli, a former prisoner from Nur Shams refugee camp. Israeli forces drive away Palestinian landowners and Israeli activists attempting to plant olive trees in Idna, north of Hebron, occupied West Bank, 18 November 2026 (Hazem Bader/AFP)",
    preview: "Israeli forces detain recently released prisoners in West Bank raids Israeli forces have raided homes and arrested several Palestinians, including recently released prisoners, across the occupied West Bank, according to the Palestinian news agency Wafa. At dawn, soldiers arrested Muadh Nader Sawafta, 23, in the village of Tubas, and Naji Ibrahim Bisharat, 50, in the nearby town of Tammun, south of Tubas. Kamal Bani Odeh, director of the Palestinian Prisoners Society in Tubas, said that Sawafta had been released from Israeli detention two months ago.",
    body: "Israeli forces detain recently released prisoners in West Bank raids Israeli forces have raided homes and arrested several Palestinians, including recently released prisoners, across the occupied West Bank, according to the Palestinian news agency Wafa. At dawn, soldiers arrested Muadh Nader Sawafta, 23, in the village of Tubas, and Naji Ibrahim Bisharat, 50, in the nearby town of Tammun, south of Tubas.\n\nKamal Bani Odeh, director of the Palestinian Prisoners Society in Tubas, said that Sawafta had been released from Israeli detention two months ago. Israeli forces had detained 20 young men from the two villages the previous night, most of them from Tubas, before releasing them, the report said. In a separate raid on Friday, Israeli forces arrested three Palestinians in Qarawa Bani Hassan, southwest of Nablus.\n\nOne of them was a former prisoner who had been released just two days earlier after spending two years in Israeli prisons, according to Wafa. Earlier on Friday, soldiers raided homes in the Iktaba neighbourhood, east of Tulkarem, and arrested three Palestinians. Local sources identified one of them as Jihad al-Qazli, a former prisoner from Nur Shams refugee camp. Israeli forces drive away Palestinian landowners and Israeli activists attempting to plant olive trees in Idna, north of Hebron, occupied West Bank, 18 November 2026 (Hazem Bader/AFP)",
